**[Critical]** Deleting the `failedAttempts` counter at `MAX_FAILED_ATTEMPTS` allows the notification to re-enter the retry path indefinitely when the cursor does not advance in the same poll, producing duplicate error comments. — Failure scenario: Notification A gives up after 5 failures, counter is deleted, `continue` skips `firstError`. But notification B in the same batch fails transiently, setting `firstError`. The `throw firstError` at the end prevents cursor advancement. Next poll: A reappears with no counter — starts from zero. After 5 more failures, another `postErrorComment` posts a **duplicate** error comment on the same thread.

```suggestion
        // Mark as permanently abandoned instead of deleting,
        // so the counter survives a cursor-non-advancing throw.
        attempts[nKey] = -1;
        continue;
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

在 `MAX_FAILED_ATTEMPTS` 时删除 `failedAttempts` 计数器，当同一批次中其他通知导致 cursor 无法推进时，允许该通知无限重新进入重试路径，产生重复错误评论。

</details>

