discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** `fakeServer.close()` is outside a `try/finally` block here (and at line ~831 in "should handle abort after close"), while every other test in this file (13 instances) correctly places it inside `finally`. These are the edge-case tests that deliberately exercise multiple-close and abort-after-close paths — exactly the paths most likely to throw.

Failure scenario: if `q.close()` or `controller.abort()` throws unexpectedly, `fakeServer.close()` is never reached, leaking the HTTP server and its bound port.

```suggestion
        try {
          await q.close();
          await q.close();
          await q.close();
        } finally {
          await fakeServer.close();
        }
```

