discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Suggestion]** If one `dispose()` call throws, remaining disposables are not cleaned up.

— Concrete cost: When the bridge terminates and the finally block runs cleanup, if `dataDisposable.dispose()` throws (e.g., the PTY's event listener removal fails), the for-loop exits immediately and `resizeDisposable.dispose()` is never called. This leaves the resize event listener attached after the bridge has torn down.

```suggestion
      for (const disposable of disposables.splice(0)) {
        try {
          disposable.dispose();
        } catch {
          // Continue disposing remaining items
        }
      }
```

<details><summary>中文说明</summary>

如果某个 `dispose()` 调用抛出异常，剩余的 disposable 不会被清理。建议在循环中加 try/catch 确保所有 disposable 都被处理。

</details>

