discussion_comments.comment_body:
**[Critical]** `decodeProcessOutput` creates `new TextDecoder(getCachedEncodingForBuffer(buffer))` without try/catch — throws `RangeError` on unsupported OEM code pages, crashing 15+ unprotected call sites.

Failure scenario: On Windows with code page 437 (US English), 850 (Western European), or 852 (Central European), `getSystemEncoding()` returns `'cp437'`/`'cp850'`/`'cp852'`. These are not WHATWG encoding labels — `new TextDecoder('cp437')` throws `RangeError`. Every CLI call site migrated from `data.toString()` to `decodeProcessOutput(data)` (clipboardUtils ×4, commandUtils, mermaidImageRenderer ×2, sox-recorder, arecord-recorder, detect-terminal-theme, sandbox ×5) has no try/catch. Additionally, `cleanup()` in `shellExecutionService.ts:1429-1433` calls this function without protection — on throw, the shell-execution promise is never resolved, hanging the caller indefinitely.

The diff's own streaming-mode decoder creation at `shellExecutionService.ts:908-915` already has the correct pattern.

```suggestion
export function decodeProcessOutput(buffer: Buffer): string {
  if (buffer.length === 0) return '';
  try {
    return new TextDecoder(getCachedEncodingForBuffer(buffer)).decode(buffer);
  } catch {
    return new TextDecoder('utf-8').decode(buffer);
  }
}
```

